Z||000005||JasonC||01-15-2001||10:54 PM||||Are there any type of headers that will fit on a V8 in the Fiero? I am guessing a type like you would find on a 3.8L? Similar to what late model W-Bodys have.<P>Thanks<P><P>------------------<BR>Jason Carmichael<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net2/smile-r.gif"> <A HREF="http://www.getpaid2surf.net/97GPGT" TARGET=_blank>My GP GT on the net.</A> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net2/smile-l.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000006||Archie||01-15-2001||11:14 PM||||At this time the only headers that will "Bolt-on" to a V-8 Fiero without modifications is the Sanderson p/n CC90.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-313s.jpg"> <P>Here is a 385 "Fast Burn" Chevy crate engine, that we are just finishing up. It has the Chevy "Hot Cam" kit with 1.6 roller rockers & the Sanderson Headers.<P>This picture was taken about 10 days ago. We test drove the car yesterday and today and it's plenty quick.<P>Archie||||reg||1
